Package: ECLIPSE
Title: ECLIPSE: Enhanced CLonotypic Inference via Prediction of Single-cell Expression
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ethan", "Burns", comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0009-8061-3686"), email = "ethan.burns@yale.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Zhaochen", "Ye", comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0000-4422-3861"), email = "zhaochen.ye@yale.edu", role = "ctb"),
    person("Kelly", "Street", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6379-5013"), email = "kelly.street@gmail.com", role = "ctb"),
    person("David", "Braun", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4543-5553"), email = "david.braun@yale.edu", role = c("aut", "fnd")))
Description: This package primary analyzes single-cell T cell receptor sequencing data (scTCR-seq) produced from the CellRanger V(D)J pipeline. Specifically, it handles ambiguous clonotypes from T cells that have <2 or >2 TCR chains. The implementation of the E-M algorithm from VDJdive is used and combined with the discrimination of clonotypes with extra TCR chains from biological expression vs. technical artifacts. The package uses and returns a Seurat object, which then is able to be filtered based on TCR chain count using a second function.
